      "id": "GENUS_REMIZ",
      "name": "Remiz",
      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "The penduline tits — tiny, acrobatic passerines named for their remarkable hanging nests, woven from plant fibres and spider silk into a pouch suspended from the tip of a thin branch. The Eurasian Penduline Tit weaves an elaborate flask-shaped nest with a false entrance and a hidden side chamber for the eggs. Males build multiple nests and females select the best one.",
      "lineage": "Eurasian Penduline Tits",
      "children": [
