          "continents": [
            "Europe"
          ],
          "subspeciesCount": 4,
          "description": "The Eurasian penduline tit or European penduline tit is a passerine bird of the genus Remiz. It is relatively widespread throughout the western Palearctic. It is migratory in the northern part of its range but resident in the southern part.",
